                <pb facs="0300" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg198"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>No official record of this conversation has been found. The information set forth
                    above is derived from the account in Alanbrooke (p. 514) which indicates that
                    Hopkins persuaded Churchill to give up his attempt to obtain a radical revision
                    of the Final Report and to settle, instead, for some minor changes. Churchill
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hinge of Fate</hi>, p. 810) recalls having been
                    warned by Hopkins of the futility of pressing his recommendations regarding
                        post-<hi rendition="#small-caps">Husky</hi> operations.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
